--- Finding (sealed_classes_and_methods): a struct declared twice in one program is not
--- refused, and the two modes disagree:
---   crow run -i: prints P[a = 1, b = 2] (the second declaration silently wins)
---   crow run:    error[E0428]: the name `P` is defined multiple times --> src/main.rs
---                error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused
---                what Crow accepted, a bug in Crow
--- Expected: refused before the program runs, in both modes, at the second declaration
--- ('P' is already a record of this program, line 11) — "Names Are Never Ambiguous".
--- (The same with a function declared twice runs alike in both modes, the later one
--- silently winning: sealed_classes_and_methods-2.co.)
struct P [a]
struct P [a, b]
log[P[1, 2]]
